{
  "id": "batchtopk-sae",
  "title": "BatchTopK sparse autoencoder",
  "description": "Replace the per-sample TopK activation with a batch-level one: keep the batch size times k largest activations across the whole batch. Inputs that contain more features can use more latents and simple inputs fewer, with the same average sparsity. Prediction: in a setting where the number of active features varies a lot (children only fire with parents), the dictionary recovers the planted features at least as well as a per-sample TopK SAE.",
